author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Alias shim records per-alias hit counters (alias, canonical, count, last_seen) in the local telemetry store honoring existing telemetry disable env-vars; canonical spellings incur zero overhead; a diagnostics surface lists alias usage and zero-use aliases; the deprecation ADR documents the zero-use-for-N-releases removal criterion; unit test proves counter increment on alias resolution and absence on canonical invocation"
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Added consented safe-integer alias counters, bounded lock waits, complete-spelling attribution, and retention pruning that rechecks the on-disk state under lock before writing, preserving concurrent telemetry clear."
expected_result: Deprecated alias diagnostics remain accurate and private while canonical and permanent commands remain uncounted; stats never recreates telemetry state after clear.
actual_result: Second Greptile race reproduced and fixed with two competing-writer regressions. Linked snapshot test passed 31 cases; full suite passed 9409 at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage.
