comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-28T22:03:17.639Z","harness:codex","Implemented local consented daily alias usage counters, zero-use diagnostics, retention pruning, and concurrent state-write serialization. Canonical invocation remains uncounted; DO_NOT_TRACK and disabled consent return no observation. Linked snapshot test passed 27 assertions across unit and CLI integration. Full suite: 9405 passed, exact coverage 100/100/100/100. Zero local use is not global removal proof; GA removal threshold remains with pm-agou."
  "2026-09-28T22:40:46.201Z","harness:codex","PR #1344 review findings: Greptile flagged executable prefixes, parent --global before a permanent extension subcommand, and foreground lock wait. CodeRabbit flagged safe-integer overflow and on-disk retention after reporting cutoff. Reproducing and correcting valid cases in the same PR before re-close."
  "2026-09-28T23:06:45.648Z","harness:codex","PR #1344 review pass: Greptile executable-prefix and parent-scope permanent-alias findings reproduced and fixed; foreground alias writes now use a 250 ms lock wait. CodeRabbit safe-integer overflow was valid and both daily and rolled-up totals now saturate. Diagnostics reads prune expired local observations when lock available and return a filtered view promptly under contention. Linked snapshot test passed 29 cases; full suite passed 9407 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. A transient unrelated cold-read performance ceiling failed under host load, then passed in isolation and on the successful full rerun."
  "2026-09-28T23:28:26.936Z","harness:codex","Second review pass: Greptile identified a cross-process clear/prune race. Stats reads an expired view, then waits for the telemetry lock; if clear removes state meanwhile, pruning must re-read under lock and avoid writing a new empty state file."
  "2026-09-28T23:41:31.078Z","harness:codex","PR #1344 second Greptile finding fixed: stats now re-reads state under the telemetry lock and skips a prune write when a concurrent clear removed state or a peer already pruned it. Controlled competing-writer tests cover both races. Linked snapshot test passed 31 cases; full suite passed 9409 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
